  "text": "Start a new adventure? This adventure will be kept in a local archive.\n\nPip told Grandma the message prepared for her after talking with Mara.\n\nIndividual musical sounds; in another setting, short written messages.\n\nSol says: “Thank you for listening. I’ll keep working on the ending.”\n\nSol is here. Let Mara walk across the secured footbridge to join you.\n\nLaunch the seed boat, then steer around the rock to the blue landing.\n\nPip and Mara are at the dock. Mara has the copy and is still on duty.\n\nThe picture is unavailable. The story and all choices are still here.\n\nPip and Grandma planted the same seed together. Pip kept his promise.\n\nMove this section away from the seed boat’s route before turning it.\n\nSharing this page with Grandma begins the telling in the game world.\n\nIt’s good to hear the stories after a day of listening for the boat.\n\nThe festival where children share stories and things they have made.\n\nPip delivered Grandma’s copy of The Empty Bench to Mara at the dock.\n\nPip and Grandma planted the same seed together in the garden’s soil.\n\nLoop, the cream and teal rolling projector beside the story screen.\n\nLet Sol walk from the workshop to the garden. Mara remains at work.\n\nVisit Mara at the dock. She needs to finish helping her passengers.\n\nThis flower is waiting for Sol to share his story at the gathering.\n\nUse Move earlier and Move later, or the up and down arrow keys, for\n\nPip helps divide the dough. Rina shapes three similar-sized loaves.\n\nThese are prepared words. Your own draft stays in its writing area.\n\nYour plan is chosen. Tell Mara and Sol so they know what to expect.\n\nReally; as it happened, rather than only being imagined or planned.\n\nPeople or things already mentioned, or something belonging to them.",
